<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia names Telstra accountants.</title>
<headline>Australia names Telstra accountants.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Finance Minister John Fahey said on Wednesday that Coopers and Lybrand and Price Waterhouse had been appointed official accountants for the partial sale of state telecommunications giant Telstra Corp.</p>
<p>Coopers and Lybrand will be the government's chief adviser and Price Waterhouse will prepare financial forecasts, review past data and be involved in the due diligence process, Fahey said in a statement.  </p>
<p>Coopers and Lybrand will advise the government on strategic and financial aspects of the Telstra sale, including the company's accounting policies, planning, systems and reporting, Fahey said.</p>
<p>The government hopes to raise at least A$8 billion from the sale of one-third of Telstra in calendar 1997.</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
